{
  "borough": "London Borough of Barking and Dagenham",
  "application_type": "All Other",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development would result in the loss of a larger family sized dwellinghouse.&amp;nbsp;This would be detrimental to the borough&#x27;s stock of family-sized dwellinghouses, the need for which is set out in the development plan and supporting evidence.&amp;nbsp;The provision of two smaller flats is not considered sufficient to justify this, particularly noting that there would be no increase in bedrooms and the flats would not provide a high quality of accommodation. The harm caused by way of a reduction in the borough&#x27;s supply of family sized dwellinghouses significantly and demonstrably outweighs the benefits of the proposed flats.&amp;nbsp;As such, the proposal would conflict with the following policies which seek to ensure that the borough&#x27;s housing supply meets the needs of its residents:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Chapter 5 of the National Planning Policy Framework&amp;nbsp; (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy H10 of the London Plan (March 2021);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy CC1 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy BC4 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011);&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policy SP3 of the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of scale and layout, would fail to provide high quality internal and external amenity space to facilitate a good quality of accommodation. The proposal is therefore at odds with the following policies which seek to ensure that developments provide high quality living space for current and future occupiers:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Paragraph 130 of the National Planning Policy Framework (NPPF) (DLUHC, September 2023);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies D4 and D6 of the London Plan (March 2021);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies CM1 and CP3 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Core Strategy (July 2010);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies BP5, BP6, BP8 and BP11 of the&amp;nbsp;Local Development Framework (LDF) Borough Wide Development Plan Document (DPD) (March 2011);&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style=&quot;&quot;&gt;Policies SP3, DMD1 and SP2 of&amp;nbsp;the London Borough of Barking and Dagenham’s Draft Local Plan 2037 (Regulation 19 Submission Version, December 2021).&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The garden spaces provided does not meet the requirements set out by&amp;nbsp;external amenity space, as such both flats provide inadequate amount of external amenity space and fall short by ~6 and ~9 sqm and are unacceptable and are contrary to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;Policy BP5 - External Amenity Space&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;The design of the proposed dwelling and the location of the refuse and cycle stores are considered to be unacceptable and inadequate, in the case of Flat 1.&amp;nbsp;Additionally, it is unclear how this could be reasonably accommodated elsewhere on site given the constrained nature of the front with the parking arrangements. As such is contrary to:&lt;/p&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Paragraph 3.3.18 and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;Policy T5 (Cycling) of the London Plan&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy BR9 (Parking) and&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy BR15 (Sustainable waste management)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the Borough Wide Policies DPD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Policy DMT 3 (Cycle parking) and&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size:11pt&quot;&gt;Part 3 in Policy DMSI 8 (Demolition, construction and operational waste)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;of the draft Local Plan 2037&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;"
  ],
